---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import DownloadButton from '../components/DownloadButton.astro';
import Faq from '../components/Faq.astro';
import Closing from '../components/Closing.astro';
import DraftNote from '../components/DraftNote.astro';
import { NAME, RELEASES_URL } from '../brand';
import { faqFor } from '../data/faq';

// The free-forever list (pricing-and-business §2.2), in four groups.
const free = [
  {
    title: 'Dictation',
    items: [
      'Unlimited dictation, in any app',
      'Every speech model, on your graphics card or processor',
      'AI cleanup on your PC',
      'The dictionary, snippets and transforms',
      'History and stats, kept on your PC',
    ],
  },
  {
    title: 'AI on your terms',
    items: [
      'A model on your PC, one click to set up',
      'Your own Ollama or LM Studio server',
      'Your own key for Groq, OpenAI, Anthropic, Gemini or OpenRouter',
      'Web search, when you switch it on',
    ],
  },
  {
    title: 'Meetings',
    items: [
      'Unlimited meeting notes, recorded on your PC',
      'Summaries, action plans and tasks',
      'Calendar reminders and briefs',
      'Search and ask across every meeting',
    ],
  },
  {
    title: 'Assistant and the rest',
    items: [
      'The Voice Assistant and Chat, with documents',
      'Spoken replies and Read aloud',
      `${NAME} Link from your phone at home`,
      'The MCP server and the local API',
    ],
  },
];
---
<Layout
  title="Pricing"
  description={`${NAME} is free: no trial, no word limit, no meeting limit. Everything that runs on your PC stays free for good.`}
>
  <PageHero
    title="Free. Not a trial, not a word limit."
    lede="Everything that runs on your own PC is free, for good. No account needed."
    cta={false}
  />

  <section class="section-tight" aria-labelledby="plans-h">
    <h2 id="plans-h" class="sr-only">Plans</h2>
    <div class="wrap plans">
      <article class="card plan-free" aria-labelledby="free-h">
        <header class="plan-head">
          <div>
            <h3 id="free-h">Free</h3>
            <p class="muted">For everyone, for everything that runs on your PC.</p>
          </div>
          <p class="price"><span class="num">£0</span><span class="muted small">Also $0 and €0. There’s nothing to pay.</span></p>
        </header>
        <div class="free-groups">
          {free.map((g) => (
            <div>
              <h4>{g.title}</h4>
              <ul class="ticks">
                {g.items.map((i) => <li>{i}</li>)}
              </ul>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
        <div class="btn-row mt-4">
          <DownloadButton size="lg" primary />
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="later" aria-labelledby="pro-h">
        <p><span class="tag">Not available yet</span></p>
        <h3 id="pro-h">Pro, later</h3>
        <p>A paid plan may come one day, and if it does it will sell only things that run on servers: AI on our key with nothing to set up, and sync between your PCs, encrypted end to end.</p>
        <ul class="promises">
          <li><strong>Nothing on the Free list will ever move to Pro.</strong></li>
          <li><strong>{NAME} will never stop working offline because of an account.</strong></li>
        </ul>
        <p class="muted small">No price yet, because there’s no plan yet. Watch the <a href={RELEASES_URL}>release notes</a> to hear first.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
    <div class="wrap mt-3">
      <DraftNote>
        For the maintainer: the free-forever wording, whether to show this Pro card at all, and whether to name a price (the business doc proposes £7 a month). The plan’s “Interested?” link goes to GitHub Discussions, which isn’t switched on for the repo, so it points at the release notes for now (plan §3.6, decision 3).
      </DraftNote>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section ruled" aria-labelledby="keys-h">
    <div class="wrap grid grid-2">
      <div class="stack">
        <h2 id="keys-h">What your own key costs</h2>
        <p>If you use a cloud AI provider, it bills you directly for what you use, at its own prices. Tidying up dictations uses very little, so for most people it’s small change. {NAME} shows each day’s usage, and an estimate of the cost, in Settings. The model on your PC costs nothing.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="stack">
        <h2>Using it at work</h2>
        <p>Go ahead. The MIT licence allows commercial use, and there are no seats to count or admin console to buy.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Faq items={faqFor('pricing')} />
  <div class="wrap">
    <DraftNote class="mb-draft">How {NAME} is funded, and whether to show a sponsor link, are the maintainer’s to answer here and on an About page (plan §3.6, §10.4).</DraftNote>
  </div>
  <Closing />
</Layout>

<style>
  .plans {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 2fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 24px;
    align-items: start;
  }
  @media (max-width: 960px) {
    .plans {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
  .plan-free {
    padding: clamp(24px, 3.5vw, 40px);
  }
  .plan-head {
    display: grid;
    gap: 18px;
    padding-bottom: 24px;
    margin-bottom: 24px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--t-rule);
  }
  .plan-head h3 {
    font-size: 1.75rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }
  .price {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 4px 16px;
  }
  .price .num {
    font-size: 4rem;
    line-height: 0.9;
  }
  .free-groups {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 28px 36px;
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .free-groups {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
  .free-groups h4 {
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 660;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }
  .free-groups .ticks {
    font-size: 0.98rem;
    gap: 8px;
  }
  .later {
    display: grid;
    gap: 14px;
    padding: clamp(22px, 3vw, 32px);
    border-radius: 16px;
    border: 1.5px dashed var(--t-border-hover);
  }
  .later h3 {
    font-size: 1.375rem;
  }
  .later > p {
    color: var(--t-fg-80);
  }
  .promises {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    padding-left: 1.1em;
  }
  .mb-draft {
    margin-bottom: 48px;
  }
</style>
